description:
Plan against docs/plans/2026-10-30-per-task-worktrees.md §2, §4 and §7 (every 'Assumed interfaces' list).

Objective: every contract the epic added is documented exactly once, in the reference docs agents and humans read, with the spelling the code uses. This is half of the epic's docs sweep, split from WT-18 for the 5-file cap.

Deliverable:
- docs/MCP_SERVER.md:
  - claim_next_task and get_context `workspace: { mode, path, branch, target }`;
  - complete_task's worktree branch policy (moe/task/<taskId>);
  - finalize_attempt outcome 'unlanded' with unlandedReason / conflictPaths / rescueRef, and the REVIEW to WORKING/BLOCKED routing.
- docs/SCHEMA.md: ProjectSettings.worktreeMode, ExecutionAttempt.workspaceMode and workspace, Task.landingRetry.
- docs/CONFIGURATION.md:
  - settings.worktreeMode (default 'off'; WT-19 flips it) and commitBoardState's worktree meaning;
  - the git-land-<target> resource declaration;
  - env MOE_WORKTREE_PATH, MOE_TASK_BRANCH, MOE_LAND_TARGET, MOE_LAND_LEASE_WAIT_SEC, MOE_WORKTREE_SWEEP_INTERVAL_SEC;
  - refs/moe/board and moe/control;
  - the new log codes with one-line meanings;
  - a pointer to the TROUBLESHOOTING runbook (WT-16).
Read the landed code, not the design doc, for final spellings. Any drift between the two gets a moe.add_comment on the slice that drifted.

NOT in scope: CLAUDE.md, scripts/CLAUDE.md, ARCHITECTURE.md and role docs (WT-18); code changes.

Verification: npm run lint && for k in worktreeMode workspaceMode landingRetry unlanded MOE_WORKTREE_PATH MOE_LAND_LEASE_WAIT_SEC MOE_WORKTREE_SWEEP_INTERVAL_SEC refs/moe/board moe/control; do grep -q "$k" docs/MCP_SERVER.md docs/SCHEMA.md docs/CONFIGURATION.md || { echo "missing $k"; exit 1; }; done

implementationPlan.description:
docs/CONFIGURATION.md, using step 1's inventory:
- Settings Reference table:
  - a worktreeMode row: its values and default 'off' (WT-19 flips it), pinned per attempt. Worktree mode needs a qualityGate, and the doctor fails 'on' without one. qualityGateScope is ignored in worktree mode, because every completion landing runs the gate.
  - commitBoardState's existing row: add its worktree meaning (board history on refs/moe/board; main never changes .moe), as landed.
- resources row: the git-land-<target> resource. Say when the wrapper takes it, that it is auto-created, and that declaring it only overrides capacity/maxLeaseMs.
- Agent Scripts env table:
  - MOE_WORKTREE_PATH, MOE_TASK_BRANCH and MOE_LAND_TARGET, which the wrapper sets for the CLI in worktree mode;
  - MOE_LAND_LEASE_WAIT_SEC, MOE_WORKTREE_SWEEP_INTERVAL_SEC and MOE_LAND_NET_BACKOFF_SEC, with the defaults the code uses.
- A new `### Worktree mode` subsection under Project Configuration:
  - W = <top>/.worktrees/<taskId> on moe/task/<taskId>;
  - the control checkout on moe/control;
  - refs/moe/board;
  - a table of every code from step 1's inventory, one line each (log codes with their meaning, internal bridge names marked internal);
  - a pointer to the TROUBLESHOOTING runbook section WT-16 added, by its real heading.
- Where an existing sentence in these three docs states shared-mode-only behaviour as universal (for example, landing onto consolidationBranch / moe/work-<date>), add a short shared-mode qualifier that points to the new subsection. Do not rewrite those passages; the broader docs sweep is WT-18.
Budget: at most 300 net added lines across the three docs.

comments.content:
Contract additions from the WT-S revision after QA reject 1. The source is the Assumed interfaces in revised §2 and §7 of docs/plans/2026-10-30-per-task-worktrees.md. Document each of these once:
- finalize_attempt `unlandedReason` value `remote`;
- env MOE_LAND_NET_BACKOFF_SEC (default 5);
- the receipt journal push result `push unknown: <detail>`, with `pushed` omitted while the outcome is unknown;
- the codes MOE_LAND_MIRROR_SKIPPED, MOE_PUSH_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN, MOE_WORKTREE_GATE_INTEGRITY and MOE_MIGRATION_NO_GATE;
- the rescue reasons `remote` and `push-unknown`.

executionContract.intendedBehavior:
docs/MCP_SERVER.md, docs/SCHEMA.md and docs/CONFIGURATION.md document every worktree-mode contract the epic landed, once each, with the code's spelling:
- claim_next_task/get_context `workspace`;
- the complete_task branch rule;
- finalize_attempt 'unlanded' and its routing;
- worktreeMode, workspaceMode, AttemptWorkspace, landingRetry and UnlandedReason;
- the env vars, git-land-<target>, refs/moe/board and moe/control;
- every wrapper log code in the MOE_WORKTREE_/LAND_/CONTROL_/BOARD_ (plus PUSH_/MIGRATION_) families.
Drift between design and code is commented on the slice that landed it. No code changes.
